<!--
  De jure feudal hierarchy for the DADG feudal titles system (War of the Roses, England 1471).

  Schema:
    <Feudalism>
      <Kingdom id="..." name="..." [seat="..."] [kingClanId="..."]>
        <Duchy id="..." name="..." [seat="..."] [holderClanId="..."]>
          <County id="..." name="..." [seat="..."] [holderClanId="..."]>
            <Barony id="..." name="..." [seat="..."] [holderClanId="..."]/>
          </County>
        </Duchy>
        <County .../>  (counties may sit directly under the crown)
      </Kingdom>
    </Feudalism>

  - "id" is required and must be unique across all titles.
  - "seat" is the StringId of the settlement that is the title's seat; it must be unique and
    must match a settlement StringId defined in the game/module data. It is optional for kingdoms.
  - "kingClanId"/"holderClanId" is the StringId of the clan initially holding the title; optional.

  Seats and holders mirror DellarteDellaGuerraMap\ModuleData\settlements.xml: every county is
  seated at one of the 28 towns, every barony at a castle, and each title's initial holder is
  its seat settlement's owner clan. The six duchies are seated at castles held by the duke's
  clan. The crown is seatless: London is held as a county so its de jure status survives a
  change of dynasty on the throne (1471 Readeption: Henry VI of Lancaster).
-->
